# Self-Boss

Self-Boss is a Windows-only local desktop MVP for turning focused work into controlled access to high-dopamine activities.

The MVP is intentionally local-only:

- Python 3.10+
- PySide6 Widgets, not QML
- SQLite only for future persistence
- pytest only for tests
- PyInstaller only for packaging
- no cloud, backend, web stack, Docker, Electron, Tauri, or mobile code

## Safety Principles

Self-Boss may eventually block apps or websites, but the bootstrap contains no real blocker logic.

Required safety rules:

- Test mode is mandatory and must be the development default.
- Recovery mode is mandatory and must work even if the GUI fails.
- Every blocker action must be reversible.
- Every system-level change must be marker-based.
- Recovery files, recovery tests, and safe-mode logic must never be removed or weakened.
- Real enforcement stays deferred until recovery tooling and tests exist.

## Deferred Work

The browser extension/native connector and guardian service are explicitly deferred. Placeholders live under `deferred/` so future work has a home without activating any system integration.

## Local Setup

```powershell
py -3.10 -m venv .venv
.\.venv\Scripts\python -m pip install --upgrade pip
.\.venv\Scripts\python -m pip install -e . -r requirements-dev.txt
```

## Run Checks

```powershell
.\.venv\Scripts\python -m pytest -q
.\.venv\Scripts\python -m selfboss.main
```

The module entry point currently prints a harmless startup message and exits without changing the system.
